WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:05.190
If you're a fan of big movies, you've probably
got a neatly-organized laundry list of films

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.100
to catch this year.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.620
From Star Wars: The Last Jedi to Wonder Woman,
all the big flicks you won't want to miss

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.280
are committed to your memory.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.550
But with all that focus on blockbusters, a
ton of amazing picks may have slipped under

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.120
your radar.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.280
Here are some of the underappreciated movie
gems from 2017 that you just need to add to

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.520
your list and watch as soon as possible.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.620
The Girl with All the Gifts

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.970
The zombie genre has been crowded for decades,
and in the post-Walking Dead era, it's only

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:32.980
grown more popular.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.820
It's hard to come up with a new spin on those
shambling undead tropes, but The Girl with

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:40.040
All the Gifts somehow manages to do it anyway.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.960
Adapted from M.R. Carey's novel, the story
imagines a world in which much of the human

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:50.280
population has been wiped out by a fungus-borne
zombie plague — yes, just like in the video

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.340
game, The Last of Us.

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:56.460
But in The Girl with all the Gifts, second-generation
victims retain their human characteristics

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.700
even as they're consumed by a hunger for flesh,
instead of turning into one of these …

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.760
Oh no — the nightmares are going to come
back ....

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.200
In The Girl with all the Gifts, which saw
a limited release in the US early in the year,

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.700
the surface-level humanity poses a moral conundrum
for a teacher tasked with educating the so-called

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.300
"hungries."

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.999
And that's compounded by the harsh utilitarian
views of the doctor in command, played by

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.900
Glenn Close.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.900
Like the best zombie horror, The Girl with
all the Gifts is underlined with thought-provoking

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:33.320
and existential questions about modern society
and human nature … and it's also an insane

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.040
thrill ride.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:36.280
The Red Turtle

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.829
Sweeping and life-affirming, this film is
by Studio Ghibli — yup, the same studio

00:01:41.829 --> 00:01:43.400
that made My Neighbor Totoro.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.080
The Red Turtle doesn't have a single sentence
of dialogue - and that gives it a pinprick

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.480
intensity that'll keep your eyes glued to
the screen the entire time.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.220
The movie centers around an unnamed man shipwrecked on a deserted tropical island, who later encounters

00:01:57.229 --> 00:01:58.710
a giant red turtle.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.240
But it's far more than what it seems superficially.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:06.600
It dives deep into the tenderness and tribulations
of what it means to be human, recounting milestones

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.750
and memory markers set over gorgeous animated
design aesthetics and an incredible score.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:16.130
While our nameless protagonist was set adrift
by a storm, we follow along the poignant plot

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:21.220
and engrossing layout until we're turned inside
out at the film's climax — one that builds

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.600
and bursts without warning.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.950
The Red Turtle is truly an experience.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.780
It's utterly captivating for its characters,
clues, and cry-inducing resolution.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.120
An absolute must-watch.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.440
The Autopsy of Jane Doe

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.800
Starring Brian Cox and Emile Hirsch as Tommy
and Austin Tilden, The Autopsy of Jane Doe

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:43.670
brings in frights and freakish encounters
from the get-go and doesn't let up until viewers

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.090
are totally spooked.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:49.940
The father-son duo in the film have an unusual
bond: they both work as coroners.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:53.920
While that alone is pretty strange, things
get far more sinister when the Tildens are

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.510
delivered the corpse of an unidentified woman
— one that shows increasingly strange signs

00:02:58.510 --> 00:02:59.510
of trauma.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.510
Who is this woman?

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:01.010
What happened to her?

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.160
Is she even dead?

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:11.320
The Autopsy of Jane Doe sizzles with uneasiness
and oddities, with a peppering of jump scares

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.510
and gory slashings.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:15.760
It all bubbles over into a climax you won't
see coming.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.020
Justice League Dark

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.270
You might have been too distracted by the
blockbuster Marvel and DC releases coming

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:25.220
this year to see Justice League Dark — which
is a shame.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.920
The Warner Bros.-backed animated flick offers
up a refreshing angle on the standard superhero

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:30.420
storylines.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:35.740
It blends together razor-sharp wit and a lot
of screentime for everyone's favorite trenchcoated

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.380
troublemaker, John Constantine.

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:42.960
As the title implies, Justice League Dark
is, well, much darker than your typical comic

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.660
book movie.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:49.120
It's got a risky R rating from the MPAA, and
it ventures into new territory beyond the

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.880
stock points fans have become almost too familiar
with.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:56.320
It maintains a quick pace and sets up a spine-tingling
whodunit mystery.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.740
But it doesn't rest on shock for shock's sake
or any fluff that falls flat.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:04.210
Though Constantine's trademark rapid-fire
swearing is absent from the film, it's one

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:07.320
that's absolutely worth a watch… now that
you know it exists.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:08.400
You're welcome.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:09.580
The Lure

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:15.000
Though this perfectly odd Polish flick saw
an international release in 2015, it finally

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.780
hit the States in February 2017, and it's
hard to express how great that is for film

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.280
fans.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:25.420
A mashup of musical camp and horror gore,
sprinkled with classic movie monsters in vampires

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:29.900
and mermaids, The Lure is wicked and weird
right down to its flippy fish tail.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.340
What's the premise, you ask?

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.699
Well, it's plot centers around mermaid-vampires-turned-strippers
—

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.699
"Shut up and take my money!"
— who attempt to lead normal lives, even

00:04:38.699 --> 00:04:40.610
under the neon lights of a nightclub.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:45.310
But their thirst for blood, sex, and violence
causes rifts in their relationships, and also

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.539
hurts their chances of staying stealthy.

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:52.830
The Lure is deliciously dicey with its characters
and turns on a dime with its disjointed scenes.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.479
But that's what makes it so gripping.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.379
It's no teeny-bopper Aquamarine dream, that's
for sure:

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.240
Maybe you could meet me in Fiji sometime?"

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.960
"Uh huh!"

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.520
"Blaaaaaaaaaaaaah"

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.140
XX

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:13.320
If there's two things horror filmmakers love,
it's anthologies and possessed children.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.919
This Sundance Film Festival gem brings together
both in a blood-boiling marriage.

00:05:17.919 --> 00:05:22.990
The brainchild of a group of female directors
— Including St. Vincent, the indie rock

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.289
goddess - her real name is Annie Clark, by
the way - — XX is comprised of four horror

00:05:27.289 --> 00:05:28.289
mini-films.

00:05:28.289 --> 00:05:33.270
The short stories weave through familial relations
of mother and son, past animalistic behaviors

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:38.169
and into mental illnesses, and deep beyond
the grit and gore of camping trips gone wrong.

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:40.909
XX finds its strengths in its subtle silliness.

00:05:40.909 --> 00:05:45.510
While scary enough in their own right, the
short tales are intercut with haunting stop-motion

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:49.711
cutscenes that bring it all together- but
there's still an element of campiness to it

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:50.840
- it just all works.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.700
A Monster Calls

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:57.340
Looking at the poster for A Monster Calls
you might be tempted to assume it's just another

00:05:57.349 --> 00:06:01.270
young adult movie about a kid who hangs around
with a talking tree monster.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:04.860
And hey, we already have the Guardians of
the Galaxy, so who needs that?

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:11.060
The reality, however, is far more complex
and compelling: the film, which saw limited

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:16.680
release in 2016 before opening wide this year,
tells the story of a 12-year-old boy struggling

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:20.970
to cope with his mother's terminal illness
while facing bullies at school and a prickly

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.060
grandmother at home.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:26.740
Dark and honest in a way that family-friendly
features rarely dare to be these days, A Monster

00:06:26.749 --> 00:06:30.219
Calls was perhaps destined to fall through
the cracks in theaters.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:32.840
But it received heaps of praise from critics
for a reason.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:33.900
Don't miss it.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.220
To the Bone

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.400
Minimalistic but moving, To the Bone tells
a tale of illness and isolation.

00:06:40.409 --> 00:06:44.490
It follows Ellen, played by Lily Collins,
a headstrong young woman who's been grappling

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.160
with anorexia for most of her life.

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:52.080
Enter Dr. William Beckham, played by an impeccably
cast Keanu Reeves, who runs an eccentric wellness

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:54.360
clinic — and runs Ellen past her wits' end.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:59.800
Directed by Buffy the Vampire Slayer writer/producer
Marti Noxon, To the Bone is black comedy at

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:04.590
its best and most beautiful, full of crackling
humor and sharp-tongued sarcasm.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:09.539
Netflix was so enamored with Noxon's directorial
debut, the streaming service snatched up the

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.700
rights to it back in January for a cool eight
million dollars.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:14.800
Soon, you'll have no excuse to miss it.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:16.240
Lovesong

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:21.520
So Yong Kim's Lovesong weaves a warm account
of two women on the cusp of self-discovery.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:26.360
Mindy and her best friend Sarah embark on
an impromptu road trip and are soon confronted

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.039
with emotions they can't deny.

00:07:28.039 --> 00:07:33.800
Kim's past credits include incredibly introspective
films such as In Between Days, For Ellen,

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.120
and Treeless Mountain, and she brings the
same kind of intricate and intimate details

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.639
to this affecting drama.

00:07:39.639 --> 00:07:43.789
Lovesong is a treat for your heart as much
as your eyes, with its gauzy pastel palette

00:07:43.789 --> 00:07:45.259
and elegant landscape.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:47.880
It'll leave you breathless at even the smallest
moments.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.760
20th Century Women

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:55.840
Set in 1979, this indie darling features an
eclectic cast of characters that includes

00:07:55.849 --> 00:08:00.809
Annette Bening as liberal leftist Dorothea,
Greta Gerwig as spunky red-haired photographer

00:08:00.809 --> 00:08:05.860
Abbie, and rebel without a cause Julie — portrayed
by a rough-around-the-edges Elle Fanning.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.460
These unique women come together to help raise
Dorothea's son ...

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.960
"Wondering if you're happy it's a great shortcut
to just being depressed."

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:18.160
This dramedy written and directed by Mike
Mills is a coming-of-age film that disregards

00:08:18.169 --> 00:08:19.330
age altogether.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:23.719
It brings to light the idea that it's never
too late to start over, start for the first

00:08:23.719 --> 00:08:26.570
time, or start believing you can begin in
the first place.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:31.229
With an engaging slice-of-life premise and
pleasing honesty, the film ebbs and flows

00:08:31.229 --> 00:08:31.760
organically.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.699
Just be sure to have some tissues on hand,
since it's pretty much guaranteed you'll get

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:36.400
misty-eyed.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:38.020
A United Kingdom

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:44.060
Amma Asante sits in the director's seat for
this 1940s foray into racial conflicts, family

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:48.300
ties, and political motivations in a time
of high tension and segregation.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:53.480
David Oyelowo and Rosamund Pike star as an
incumbent African king and lily-white Londoner

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:54.540
Ruth Williams.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:58.920
The pair falls deep and fast for one another,
much to the chagrin of those around them.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:03.570
Dodging attempts to break them apart and prevent
them from eloping, the duo is pushed to defy

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.180
odds and never back down.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:10.420
From screenwriter Guy Hibbert, A United Kingdom
is at once powerful and appropriately uniting,

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:14.620
piloting through the nooks and crannies of
love and liberty to present a raw account

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.220
of a couple battling adversity.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:20.910
Though the film does lean away from the grittier
elements of racism, Hibbert crafts a potent

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.600
story that will leave any viewer changed for
the better.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.080
Kedi

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:29.180
Next up on the list of films you've missed
is possibly the one you'll be most bummed

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:30.610
you didn't know existed.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:34.149
This is the Internet, and as such, cats are
worshipped as gods.

00:09:34.149 --> 00:09:37.550
Kedi is a documentary about the feral cats
of Istanbul.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:42.170
The filmmakers took to the streets to introduce
viewers to the free-roaming felines that lead

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:46.550
surprisingly unique lives and the people who
interact with them on a daily basis.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:51.050
Kedi features kittens with knacks for slipping
into hidden alleyway crevices, cats that keep

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:55.680
a keen eye on the docks for the incoming fish
market shipments, and furry-faced friends

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:58.280
perched upon doorsteps and behind shop counters.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:03.240
It can be silly on the surface, but Kedi has
a big heart, and though it's centered around

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.149
animals, the film's narrative feels utterly
human.

00:10:06.149 --> 00:10:10.920
Very much a part of the local culture and
the community of Istanbul, the cats and kittens

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:15.290
of Kedi remind us all that we're not born
knowing hatred or judgment, illustrated through

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:17.850
the remarkable respect between man and animal.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:18.340
Plus?

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.340
Adorable kittens!

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:20.280
What's not to love?

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:21.380
Thanks for watching!

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.620
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:26.980
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love!

